# Configuration

`nml.toml`, at the root of a workspace, configures it. Every key has a default: an empty file is a valid workspace. A key NML does not know is an error, so a typo does not go unnoticed. This documentation's:

:lua`nml.element("code_block", { code = nml.read("/nml.toml"), numbers = false })`

## Pages {#pages}

| Key | Default | |
|:----|:--------|:-|
| `pages` | `["**/*.nml"]` | Patterns of the files that are pages, relative to the root. |
| `exclude` | `[]` | Patterns of files that are not pages, even if `pages` matches them. |
| `output` | `"public"` | Where pages are written, relative to the root. |
| `database` | `".nml/index.db"` | The workspace's [[building#index|index]], relative to the root. |

The other `.nml` files are libraries: see [[documents#libraries]]. Patterns are globs: `*` matches within a directory, `**` across directories.

## HTML {#html}

The `[html]` section configures the pages around the content.

| Key | Default | |
|:----|:--------|:-|
| `language` | none | The `lang` of every page, such as `"en"`. |
| `stylesheets` | `[]` | Stylesheets every page links to, after the default one. A relative URL is relative to the output directory. |
| `icon` | none | The URL of the pages' icon. |
| `default_style` | `true` | Whether pages link `nml.css`, the default style. |
| `code_theme` | `"InspiredGitHub"` | The colors of highlighted code. |
| `code_theme_dark` | `"base16-ocean.dark"` | The colors of highlighted code in a dark color scheme. |
| `static` | none | A directory whose files are copied as they are to the output directory, at the same paths. |

See [[style#]].

## Renderers {#render}

The `[render]` section names the programs that draw [[math-diagrams#|math and diagrams]], when they are not those on the `PATH`.

| Key | Default |
|:----|:--------|
| `latex` | `"latex"` |
| `dvisvgm` | `"dvisvgm"` |
| `dot` | `"dot"` |
| `typst` | `"typst"` |

`[render.tex.<name>]` sections are LaTeX environments: `main` is the default one, and `:tex[env=name]` picks another.

| Key | |
|:----|:-|
| `preamble` | What comes before `\begin{document}`: packages, macros. |
| `font_size` | The font size, in points. Default: 10. |
| `block_prepend` | What comes before the source of `:tex` blocks, but not math. |
| `latex` | The LaTeX program of this environment, such as `"lualatex"`. |

## Runners {#run}

Each `[run.<name>]` section is a runner of [[runners#|`:run` blocks]], named by their fence:

| Key | |
|:----|:-|
| `command` | The program and its arguments: `["Rscript", "{file}"]`. `{file}` is a file holding the code; without it, the code is the standard input. |
| `extension` | The extension of that file. Default: the runner's name. |
| `timeout` | How many seconds a run may take. Default: 300. |
| `env` | Variables added to the program's environment. |

## Modules {#modules}

Each `[[module]]` section is a root of [[documents#import|modules]]:

| Key | |
|:----|:-|
| `name` | The first part of the modules' names: `name.a.b`. A workspace's own `std` replaces the standard library. |
| `root` | The directory, relative to the workspace's root: `name.a.b` is `<root>/a/b.nml`. |

## When it changes

A change of the configuration builds every page again: it can change any of them.
